---
title: Find the returns number by ear
order: 5
summary: "The same web page twice: once as a picture, once as the words a screen reader actually has to work with."
scenario: You have bought a coat that does not fit. You are blind and you use a screen reader, so the page reaches you one announcement at a time, in order, with no way to skim. You need the returns phone number, and you need to know which of the two coats is the waterproof one.
tasks:
  - Step through the announcements one at a time. No skipping ahead, no reading the picture.
  - Write down the returns phone number and which coat is waterproof.
  - Open the links list, the way a screen reader user would to get their bearings, and see how much it tells you.
time: 10 minutes
barrier: Missing alt text, meaningless link text and no headings
criterion: WCAG 2.2 &mdash; <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/non-text-content.html">1.1.1 Non-text Content</a> and <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/link-purpose-in-context.html">2.4.4 Link Purpose</a>
script: screenreader.js
---

