    <p><strong>This is a simplification.</strong> A real screen reader runs at two or three hundred words a minute, and an experienced user moves by heading, landmark and form field rather than one item at a time. That makes the broken page worse, not better: the shortcuts they rely on are exactly what is missing.</p>
